From: BananaOS Korean contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Keep UTF-8 filenames visible in SSH/SCP listings

Noninteractive SSH clients may omit LANG or explicitly use the C locale
to parse ls timestamps. Use UTF-8 for filename display if the requested
character locale is not Unicode. Keep sanitizing invalid/control bytes.

--- a/coreutils/ls.c
+++ b/coreutils/ls.c
@@ -1101,6 +1101,10 @@
 	INIT_G();
 
 	init_unicode();
+	/* Banana stores filesystem names as UTF-8 even in noninteractive SSH. */
+	if (unicode_status != UNICODE_ON)
+		reinit_unicode("C.UTF-8");
+
 
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_LS_WIDTH
 	/* obtain the terminal width */
